# Workspace pnpm settings.
#
# public-hoist-pattern[]=tslib — @redocly/cli's CLI bootstrap eagerly imports
# all commands at startup (lint runs build-docs's require chain too); that
# chain ends at `styled-components → tslib`. pnpm's strict node_modules
# layout puts tslib under styled-components' deeply-nested .pnpm dir where
# Node's require can't reach it. Hoisting tslib to the root node_modules
# (visible to all transitive deps) fixes "Cannot find module 'tslib'" on
# `pnpm --filter @lemmaoracle/spec validate:openapi`.
#
# Repro: clean `pnpm install` on Linux CI runners with a populated lockfile
# cache exhibits the failure; local macOS dev with a fresh install often
# does not, because typescript-eslint pulls tslib up as a sibling. The CI
# behaviour is the one we ship for, so we pin the hoist.
public-hoist-pattern[]=tslib
